[1m[38;2;255;169;64marmada fleet spawn — start an isolated agent Job on a task[0m

[1m[38;2;255;169;64mUSAGE[0m
  armada fleet spawn <task> [--workflow <name>] [--name <handle>]
  armada fleet spawn <task> [--budget <k>=<v>]… [--confidence <0-1>]
  armada fleet spawn <task> [-C <path>] [--dry-run]

[1m[38;2;255;169;64mFLAGS[0m
  --workflow <name>   [38;2;156;163;175moverride classification; a workflow in your guild[0m
  --name <handle>     [38;2;156;163;175mthe Job's handle; derived from the task when absent[0m
  --budget <k>=<v>    [38;2;156;163;175moverride one ceiling, repeatable[0m
  --confidence <0-1>  [38;2;156;163;175mbelow this, stop and ask which workflow; 0 never asks[0m
  -C <path>           [38;2;156;163;175mthe repository to branch from; the cwd's when absent[0m
  --dry-run           [38;2;156;163;175mreport the plan: workflow, worktree, ports, budget[0m
  --json              [38;2;156;163;175manswer as one JSON object, for a script or an agent[0m
  --color <when>      [38;2;156;163;175mauto (default), always, never; NO_COLOR wins[0m

[1m[38;2;255;169;64mEXAMPLES[0m
  armada fleet spawn "add rate limiting to the API"
    [38;2;156;163;175mthe task is the argument: one quoted string, given up front[0m

  armada fleet spawn "port the CLI to clap" --workflow refactor
    [38;2;156;163;175mskip classification and name the workflow yourself[0m

  armada fleet spawn "audit the auth flow" -C ~/work/api --dry-run
    [38;2;156;163;175manother repository, and the plan only — nothing starts[0m

The task is required. Armada never prompts for it afterwards, so a
shell that ate your quotes is a refusal rather than an empty Job.
